146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The SRN Solar PV Project in Khaldiya is expected to provide several social benefits to the local community. One of its main advantages is the creation of jobs during the construction, installation, operation, and maintenance phases. Proper installation and long-term operation of the solar energy system will require engineers, technicians, project managers, and support staff. This can lead to additional employment opportunities and the development of technical skills in the renewable energy sector.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (Another advantage is increasing public awareness of renewable energy and sustainability. Residents may become more interested in adopting sustainable practices such as energy saving and rooftop solar systems after detecting the usage of solar panels and clean energy technologies in their region. This can help to build a stronger environmental culture in Khaldiya.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The SRN Solar PV Project may also help improve public health by reducing air pollution generated by traditional fossil-fuel power generation. Lower emissions can enhance air quality and help to prevent respiratory diseases and other pollution-related health issues. Furthermore, the SRN Solar PV Project can improve energy dependability by supplying electricity to the local grid, particularly during peak summer demand in Kuwait.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (However, some transitory issues may arise during the project's early stages. Residents may be inconvenienced by construction noise, traffic disruptions, or other factors. Some neighbourhood members may first oppose changes or be unfamiliar with renewable energy systems. Despite these limitations, the long-term social advantages are predicted to surpass the immediate difficulties.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The SRN Solar PV Project in Khaldiya requires an essential initial investment, estimated at around 59.5 million KD for an 85 MW system \(calculated from 85MW * 700,000 KD/MW\). This cost covers solar panels, inverters, electrical equipment, installation, grid connection, infrastructure development, and maintenance planning. Despite the high initial cost, solar energy projects are viewed as long-term investments with significant potential returns.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (One of the most important economic advantages is the reduction in long-term electricity generation costs. Because sunshine is a free and abundant resource in Kuwait, post-installation operational costs are significantly lower than those of typical fossil fuel power plants. This can help to lessen the long-term financial burden of electricity production while also promoting national energy savings. The project may also lessen reliance on fossil fuels such as oil and natural gas. This enables important hydrocarbon resources to be kept for export or reallocated to higher-value businesses. Furthermore, investment in renewable energy promotes economic diversity, which is a critical goal for Kuwait's future economy. Another economic benefit is the creation of local job opportunities in the engineering sector, especially for AASU graduates and majors such as Energy Systems Engineering, Environmental and Sustainability Engineering. These majors can directly contribute to the planning, operation, and development of many projects.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (According to Dr. Morsi Ahmed, one of the major challenges facing renewable energy projects in the Gulf region is the high cost of infrastructure transformation, since most existing systems were originally designed for traditional oil and gas energy sources \(M. Ahmed, personal communication, November 3, 2025\). This highlights the importance of strategic planning and phased investment when implementing the SRN Solar PV Project in Khaldiya. Although the payback period may take several years, the long-term economic benefits make the project financially beneficial and valuable.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
