/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (This estimated value reflects a very high degree of human development in Khaldiya. The SRN Solar PV Project has the potential to grow this value over time by improving health, providing improved education support, and expanding economic prospects.The SRN Solar PV Project in Khaldiya has the potential to boost the district's human development index. It may benefit health by lowering air pollution and emissions from traditional power generating. It can also help with education by providing reliable electricity to schools, laboratories, and digital learning systems. Furthermore, the project may generate job opportunities and lower long-term energy prices, hence raising income levels and living standards. Overall, the project has the potential to improve the quality of life and promote )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (long-term growth in Khaldiya.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (In conclusion, this project demonstrated that the use of photovoltaic \(PV\) solar energy is a highly effective and suitable solution for the Al-Khalidiya area. Based on the estimated annual electricity demand of approximately 289.5 GWh, these panels were designed to provide a significant portion of the residents' energy needs. Furthermore, the use of renewable energy resources such as photovoltaic solar panels is a very clean resource and represents a strong alternative to fossil fuels, which can harm the environment and cause pollution in the area. The selection of solar panels was based on studies we conducted, which found that the high solar irradiance and climatic conditions in Kuwait make solar energy a suitable and highly effective solution for generating electricity in the area. Through this project, the system is designed to cover approximately 50% of the residents' electricity requirements, demonstrating the project's success when implemented as planned.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (In addition, the project highlighted its environmental benefits in reducing greenhouse gas emissions, as well as its positive social and economic impact, including raising public awareness, creating job opportunities, and achieving long-term cost savings. The Human Development Index assessment indicated that the transition to renewable energy will contribute to comprehensive sustainable development. Overall, the results of this project study indicate that implementing photovoltaic solar energy technology in residential areas such as Al-Khalidiyah will play a key role in reducing the use of fossil fuels and achieving a more sustainable and resilient energy future.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
