/E (From a materials science point of view, there are several promising materials. First, Perovskites these materials can significantly increase the efficiency of solar panels. Second, carbon-based composites these materials are lightweight and resistant to corrosion, making them ideal for wind energy systems. Finally, MOFs, or Metal-Organic Frameworks. This material was invented by a Nobel laureate, Omar Yaghi, at the University of California, Berkeley. MOFs can store hydrogen, which makes them very important for green hydrogen production and the future of renewable energy. So, these three materials Perovskites, carbon-based composites, and MOFs are strong candidates for improving renewable energy technologies.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [23]
>>
